    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0849" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.156/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-11T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>370. Your 454, November 9, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="14" xml:id="d640-f1"/> Tangier port
                    concession.</p>
                <p>Tangier telegraphs that British Agency reports postponement until after Lausanne
                    Conference, due to Curzon’s personal plea to Poincaré. Please cable any
                    development.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d640-f1" n="14" xml:id="d640-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see Department’s telegram no. 22 to Tangier, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
